WEBVTT

00:00:00.454 --> 00:00:02.886
early in your journey
but Entrepreneurship,

00:00:02.886 --> 00:00:06.566
it is a bumpy road, but it's the
most fulfilling thing that you

00:00:06.566 --> 00:00:10.166
can do when you know you put
your all into something and then

00:00:10.166 --> 00:00:11.126
it turns up, right?

00:00:11.126 --> 00:00:13.846
Cause I've been. through the
the roles where it's like,

00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:15.542
okay. Am I gonna do this?

00:00:15.542 --> 00:00:18.022
Or like, what if the, I can't
go get an agency job and I gotta

00:00:18.022 --> 00:00:19.222
drive Amazon or something.

00:00:19.222 --> 00:00:21.542
Like, it's it's that's the
real life of an entrepreneur.

00:00:21.542 --> 00:00:23.942
Like, you know, I could come in
here and wear thousand dollars

00:00:23.942 --> 00:00:26.342
worth of things and then I lose
all my clients and I gotta sell

00:00:26.342 --> 00:00:28.846
my stuff and I'm back
to where I started.

00:00:28.966 --> 00:00:32.246
And that's that's the
reality of this role,

00:00:32.246 --> 00:00:36.230
but the fulfillment in Success of
something that you built yourself,

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:39.990
that you built with people
that you have an affinity for,

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:42.022
is unmatched. But
it's a challenge.

00:00:42.022 --> 00:00:44.982
And I feel like the biggest
challenge is when you've done all

00:00:44.982 --> 00:00:47.790
these things and you become
successful because of them.

00:00:47.846 --> 00:00:50.006
And then you don't know what to
do with them when they start to

00:00:50.006 --> 00:00:53.206
fall apart. Like it's the hardest, it's
the hardest part of entrepreneurship.

00:00:53.206 --> 00:00:54.670
And it's something you go through.

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:56.854
Um, every day, where
it's like, I couldn't,

00:00:56.854 --> 00:01:01.254
I how can I know that a song
we did four years ago was

00:01:01.254 --> 00:01:03.734
gonna blow up and win Grammys
and all of this stuff at the time

00:01:03.734 --> 00:01:05.734
where I'm like, you hear
the stories about artists,

00:01:05.734 --> 00:01:07.884
they'd be like, you know,
I don't know if y'all,

00:01:07.974 --> 00:01:10.254
what's the girl, Georgiana?

00:01:10.742 --> 00:01:12.742
The rapper girl, but
she signed her deal.

00:01:12.742 --> 00:01:15.406
She had $50. She had to call
her label to send her money.

00:01:15.462 --> 00:01:17.702
So it's like you go through
those moments where you like,

00:01:17.702 --> 00:01:19.862
even when the song blew
up, it's like we're still,

00:01:19.862 --> 00:01:23.542
it takes nine to 18 months to
see any dollars from publishing,

00:01:23.542 --> 00:01:26.022
you know, for the money, the
money, the record's making money.

00:01:26.022 --> 00:01:30.134
So it's like, you experience those
times where you feel like You

00:01:30.134 --> 00:01:33.654
have nothing and everything that
you've done got you to this space.

00:01:33.654 --> 00:01:37.198
But really, that's not true,
you know, but it feels that way.

00:01:37.254 --> 00:01:38.990
It was at times where I knew

00:01:39.462 --> 00:01:42.102
I don't come from nothing, so if
I have to operate off nothing,

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:44.038
I'm gonna be okay. Right.

00:01:44.038 --> 00:01:46.118
But that also is what drives me.

00:01:46.118 --> 00:01:50.118
I don't ever have to go through
those experiences again if I continue

00:01:50.118 --> 00:01:51.218
to just push, you
know, and so, um,

00:01:52.422 --> 00:01:55.622
Yeah, it was like When you start,
when you start from nothing,

00:01:55.622 --> 00:01:57.542
it's like, yeah, I'm
not afraid of nothing.

00:01:57.542 --> 00:02:00.422
I'm afraid of not.
making the effort to get,

00:02:00.422 --> 00:02:01.702
you know, to where
I'm trying to be.

00:02:01.702 --> 00:02:05.238
So. Yeah, it yeah, that's why I'm
like when you even if you feel

00:02:05.238 --> 00:02:06.542
down and out, it's like

00:02:07.206 --> 00:02:08.966
The you can't go no
further than the bottom,

00:02:08.966 --> 00:02:10.414
so you might as well look up.

00:02:11.558 --> 00:02:12.658
That's a bar.

00:02:13.542 --> 00:02:15.862
That's a bar. It's
really real too.

00:02:15.862 --> 00:02:17.966
I always think about that.

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:22.470
With my own journey, I started
Gray Matter with $5,000 in my bank

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:25.990
account. And I was like, it
can't get no worse than this.

00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:29.710
So any time that times are tough.

00:02:29.862 --> 00:02:33.542
There are moments where it's
just like, I learned so,

00:02:33.542 --> 00:02:34.990
I learned how to work.

00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:39.430
with so little. That like
that's not scary anymore,

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:41.806
right?

00:02:44.086 --> 00:02:46.166
For your wisdom. Thank
you for your time.

00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:49.446
Thank you for pouring back into
where it all started for you.

00:02:49.446 --> 00:02:52.396
This is a cool,
full circle moment.

00:02:52.406 --> 00:02:53.206
Yeah.
